# The Cost and Management of Program Adequacy: An Emerging Issue in Educational Policy and Finance.

**Authors:** Clune, William H.

## Abstract
Introduces a special issue on educational program adequacy--the cost of raising poor children's outcomes to functional levels through improved systems of finance, governance, organization, implementation, and educational practice. Essays raise numerous problems, including a weak knowledge base, low educational productivity, political resistance, measurement problems, weak implementation capacity, institutional design, inclusion of early childhood education and school-linked services, and state aid. (MLH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ494722

